# Line endings: LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# By default git stores LF but checks files out as CRLF on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true), so the working copy and the stored blob disagree.
# Committing part of such a file can then place hunks on the wrong lines,
# which once put added lines above the namespace and broke the build
# (see AGENTS.md). eol=lf makes checkouts LF too, so the two always match.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe mis-parses batch files that use LF only.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never rewrite binaries.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
